      "writtenOn": "2025-03-12T14:19:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Q: Does ResourceMemoryAllocator/BuddyAllocator know the exact allocation size? Of course it must know how much memory to return for suballocation. I\u0027m wondering if that isn\u0027t enough information to know the exact allocation size vs padding or something like that.",
      "revId": "de05316fb20a721193d108136f4352e2d95f9d25",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "679d8ae0_2eb86092",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/ResourceMemoryAllocation.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 64,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003581
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-12T15:50:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The BuddyMemoryAllocator suballocates memory as `NextPowerOfTwo(allocationSize)` which adds some padding but this size is not known to ResourceMemoryAllocator when incrementing mTotalUsedMemory. So I decided to just keep track of the requested exact allocation size assmuing the extra padding should be counted under Fragmentation maybe.",
      "parentUuid": "1987c588_7224eb96",
      "revId": "de05316fb20a721193d108136f4352e2d95f9d25",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
