        "id": 1003581
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-11T18:10:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We ideally want to update memory tracking when the memory is actually freed. How should we go about that, maybe callbacks? \n\nSimilar below for suballocations.",
      "revId": "de05316fb20a721193d108136f4352e2d95f9d25",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "811ec250_447b0cca",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/ResourceMemoryAllocatorVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 147,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-13T14:01:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In Vulkan we have the \"FencedDeleter\" that\u0027s used to actually free the objects. We could make it handle not just Vk* objects but also memory allocations that would be moved there? This way the memory allocation would know when it is actually no longer used.",
      "parentUuid": "d475cdf4_ce390636",
      "revId": "de05316fb20a721193d108136f4352e2d95f9d25",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "797ff18e_55279418",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/ResourceMemoryAllocatorVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 147,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-13T14:23:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  We could make it handle not just Vk* objects but also memory allocations that would be moved there? \n\nWe\u0027d have to move all the allocation tracking to FencedDeleter to make that work. Not sure on feasibility there.\n\nWith the memory usage tracking in SingleTypeAllocator we\u0027d need some way for FencedDeleter to notify STA the vkFreeAllocation() call has happened. At that point STA would decrement `mTotalAllocatedMemory`. I think FencedDeleter would essentially need a tuple `{VkDeviceMemory, VkDeviceSize, SingleTypeAllocator*}`  instead of just `VkDeviceMemory` to do that.\n\nIf `mTotalAllocatedMemory` was moved to RMA then I guess FencedDeleter could just hold a single pointer back to RMA and notify it on deletion with size. That way only `{VkDeviceMemory, VkDeviceSize}` needs to be enqueued for deletion.\n\nAlternatively RMA::Tick() already exists. RMA could hold a list of `{ExecutionSerial, VkDeviceSize}`. When this code enqueues deletion with FencedDeleter it would also push the same deletion serial (need a way to get that from FencedDeleter) and size into the list in RMA. That way when RMA::Tick() runs it can pop the corresponding entry in the list for completion serial and decrement `mTotalAllocatedMemory` by the size.",
      "parentUuid": "811ec250_447b0cca",
      "revId": "de05316fb20a721193d108136f4352e2d95f9d25",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7aeae022_98789cf0",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/ResourceMemoryAllocatorVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 159,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-12T14:19:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO it would be easier to understand if you tracked both allocated and used memory in SingleTypeAllocator. I guess the complication is that SingleTypeAllocator doesn\u0027t know used sizes for individual allocations? I guess it knows the size of the allocation, it just doesn\u0027t know if it\u0027s going to be used for future suballocation or an individual allocation.\n\nAlthough see what cwallez or lokokung think here before making changes. This might also depend on how you deal with tracking when vkFreeMemory() runs from FencedDeleter.",
      "revId": "de05316fb20a721193d108136f4352e2d95f9d25",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3739ba96_8ffcdb04",
